      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A company must first verify the identity of the requester, which is a crucial first step. If the request is valid, the company needs to assess if there are any overriding legal grounds to refuse the deletion. If not, they must then erase the personal data across all systems within the stipulated timeframe. Finally, they must inform the data subject that the data has been deleted, unless there's a legal obligation preventing that notification.",
      "source": "target",
