      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Edge cases where data lingers are precisely where the most diligent data inventory and mapping come into play. You must maintain a comprehensive data map, tracking where every piece of personal data resides, not just in the primary live systems, but also in logs, archives, and shadow databases. If data is hiding unexpectedly, it often means your initial data mapping was incomplete, which is why continuous data discovery tools are vital. Think of it like a massive, ever-growing patch of territory that needs constant surveying to find every single hidden stash of forgotten treasure—or in this case, forgotten data.",
